## Simulator verification (trio-sim plugin)

This repo's `.BAS` programs run on a headless simulator provided by the `trio-sim` plugin
(marketplace `trio-tools`, repo `maverick8969/trio-hmi-visualizer`). Use the `trio-sim` and
`trio-hmi` skills. Always pass `--bas .` so the simulator runs the code in this checkout.

After changing any `.BAS` file:
1. `--parse-only` must report 0 parse errors.
2. `--scenario all` (built-ins) and `--scenario sim/scenarios.json` (this repo's scenarios, if present) must pass.
3. For behavior changes, snapshot the VR outputs on the base commit and `--diff` against your change with
   the same inputs. List every changed VR/global in your summary and say whether it was intended.
4. If an operator-visible value changed, run `hmi-shot` on the affected HMI page(s) and look at the PNGs.

Never claim a change is verified on the sim without quoting the command and its pass/fail result.
Plant physics are illustrative — the sim verifies logic, sequencing, interlocks and VR values, not
real temperatures, flows or ramp times.
